{
 "summary": "The available metrics show no failure: gateway, orders, and inventory all report a 0% 5xx ratio, normal p95 latency (45-182ms), and steady traffic throughout the window. Nothing here explains a full checkout outage. Either the failure is outside these services and signals (for example client-side, payment, DNS/CDN, or non-5xx errors), or the incident report needs to be verified.",
 "root_cause": null,
 "contributing_factors": [],
 "timeline": [],
 "ruled_out": [
  {
   "statement": "Gateway is not returning 5xx errors or showing elevated latency. Its 5xx ratio was 0% (max 0%), p95 averaged 136ms (max 182ms), and traffic held at about 1.95 req/s.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-be0e298b6f6f"
   ]
  },
  {
   "statement": "Orders shows no server errors or latency degradation. Its 5xx ratio was 0% and p95 averaged 98ms (max 100ms).",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-ec0b0895dc48"
   ]
  },
  {
   "statement": "Inventory shows no server errors or latency degradation. Its 5xx ratio was 0% and p95 averaged 45ms (max 47ms).",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-5859ba914c39"
   ]
  },
  {
   "statement": "Traffic is still reaching the backend, so a total loss of inbound requests is not visible at the gateway. Request rate stayed between about 1.5 and 2.2 req/s.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-be0e298b6f6f",
    "ev-ec0b0895dc48",
    "ev-5859ba914c39"
   ]
  }
 ],
 "unknowns": [
  "No traces, logs, or deployment records were included in the snapshot, so error bodies, non-5xx failures (4xx, or 200 responses with error payloads), and recent changes cannot be assessed.",
  "It is unknown whether a checkout or payment service exists outside the three measured services. If it does, it has no metrics in this snapshot.",
  "The 4xx rate is not shown. Checkout could be failing with 4xx errors (for example auth or validation) that a 5xx ratio would not capture.",
  "It is unclear whether the outage is upstream of the gateway (CDN, DNS, frontend/client, load balancer) and requests never arrive. Gateway traffic continues, but a baseline to compare it against is not shown.",
  "Whether the customer reports have been confirmed with synthetic checks or real-user monitoring is unknown."
 ],
 "recommended_actions": [
  {
   "action": "Run a synthetic end-to-end checkout and capture the exact error and the component that returns it.",
   "rationale": "Backend metrics show no errors, so the failure point has to be confirmed directly.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-be0e298b6f6f"
   ]
  },
  {
   "action": "Query gateway 4xx rates and response codes by route, specifically checkout endpoints, and pull gateway and orders logs and traces for checkout requests in the window.",
   "rationale": "A 0% 5xx ratio does not rule out 4xx errors or application-level failures returned with 2xx status.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-be0e298b6f6f",
    "ev-ec0b0895dc48"
   ]
  },
  {
   "action": "Check the health of components in front of the gateway (CDN, DNS, load balancer, frontend) and of any payment or third-party dependency, and review recent deploys and config changes.",
   "rationale": "The measured services look healthy, so the cause is likely outside them or in signals not collected here.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-be0e298b6f6f",
    "ev-5859ba914c39",
    "ev-ec0b0895dc48"
   ]
  },
  {
   "action": "Compare the current request rate with the normal baseline for this time of day.",
   "rationale": "About 1.95 req/s at the gateway may be well below normal, which would point to failures upstream of the gateway.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "ev-be0e298b6f6f"
   ]
  }
 ]
}
